WEBVTT

00:00:00.007 --> 00:00:04.597
Here is a small example of a list growing as a new record arrives.

00:00:04.597 --> 00:00:11.197
The starting ages are forty-four, fifty-seven, thirty-nine, and sixty-three.

00:00:11.197 --> 00:00:16.472
We append fifty-one, so the list now contains five values.

00:00:16.472 --> 00:00:21.492
The loop then builds a second list containing only ages above fifty.

00:00:21.492 --> 00:00:26.264
That should include fifty-seven, sixty-three, and fifty-one.

00:00:26.844 --> 00:00:32.411
Notice that we are using one list as the source and another list as the filtered result.

00:00:32.411 --> 00:00:36.026
That pattern appears frequently in data preparation.

00:00:36.026 --> 00:00:40.490
These are generic fictional records, not real patient data.
